@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
}

<section class="band">
    <div class="wrap article">
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="ph-note">Draft for review. Items in [square brackets] must be completed by ECHT GROUP before launch.</p>

        <h3>1. Who we are</h3>
        <p>ECHT GROUP is a consulting company that advises businesses on marketing, strategic market development, legal and compliance, and IT. This policy explains how we handle personal information on this website.</p>

        <h3>2. What we collect</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Account details:</b> your name, email address and password. Passwords are stored in a protected, scrambled form, and we cannot read them.</li>
            <li><b>Profile details (optional):</b> title, gender, contact numbers, an alternative email, your address and a profile photo.</li>
            <li><b>Bookings:</b> the service, date, time and any notes you add.</li>
            <li><b>Messages and enquiries:</b> what you send through the Contact page, the Get started form, your Messages page and the chat assistant, together with your name and email where you give them.</li>
            <li><b>Reviews:</b> your rating and review text. Your first name and the first letter of your surname are shown publicly with it.</li>
            <li><b>Consent record:</b> the time you agreed to this policy when you registered.</li>
            <li><b>Technical data:</b> small files called cookies, described below.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3. Why we collect it</h3>
        <p>To create and secure your account, manage your bookings, reply to your messages and enquiries, direct your question to the right department, show reviews, and keep the site working safely.</p>

        <h3>4. Who can see it</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Our consultants can see messages, enquiries and bookings sent to their department. Staff accounts are restricted by role and department.</li>
            <li>Reviews, with your first name and surname initial, are visible to anyone who visits the site.</li>
            <li>We use hosting and database providers to run the site: [name the hosting provider]. We do not sell your personal information.</li>
            <li>To display fonts and icons, your browser loads files from Google Fonts and the jsDelivr network, which may receive your IP address.</li>
            <li>The chat assistant is a rule-based tool built into this site. It does not send what you type to an outside artificial intelligence service. [Update this line if that changes.]</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>5. Cookies</h3>
        <p>We use only the cookies the site needs to work: one that keeps you signed in, security tokens that protect forms, and a short-lived cookie that carries confirmation messages between pages. We do not use advertising cookies.</p>

        <h3>6. How long we keep it</h3>
        <p>[State how long accounts, messages, bookings and enquiries are kept, and what happens when an account is deleted.]</p>

        <h3>7. Keeping it safe</h3>
        <p>The site uses an encrypted connection, role-based access and protected password storage. No system is completely secure, so please use a strong, unique password and tell us if you suspect misuse of your account.</p>

        <h3>8. Your rights</h3>
        <p>You can ask to see the information we hold about you, correct it, or have it deleted, subject to any legal duty we have to keep it. You can update most of your details yourself on your profile page. For anything else, contact us at [privacy contact email]. If you are unhappy with how we handle your information, you may complain to the data-protection regulator that applies to the business: [name the regulator].</p>

        <h3>9. Children</h3>
        <p>This site is intended for businesses and adults. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

        <h3>10. Information officer</h3>
        <p>[Name and contact details of the person responsible for data protection at ECHT GROUP.]</p>

        <h3>11. Changes to this policy</h3>
        <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The date of the latest update will be shown here: [date].</p>
    </div>
</section>